      "output": {
        "rootCause": "The `is_whitespace` attribute is set to `False` for `RawSegment` instances by default in `BaseSegment.is_whitespace = False` (src/sqlfluff/core/parser/segments/base.py#L55-L90). This is a machine-protected invariant because ordinary code segments must remain non-whitespace. The `RawSegment.make` method (src/sqlfluff/core/parser/segments/raw.py#L1-L145) is used to create segment classes, and it passes `is_whitespace` as a keyword argument to the `RawSegment` class. However, the `is_whitespace` flag is not being set correctly for whitespace tokens in the `dialect_ansi` lexer (src/sqlfluff/core/dialects/dialect_ansi.py#L45-L95).",
        "confidence": 0.95,
        "evidence": [
          "src/sqlfluff/core/parser/segments/base.py#L55-L90: is_whitespace = False",
